     "probability": "high",
     "answer": "Corrosion is the gradual destruction of metals by chemical reactions with their environment, such as oxidation when iron reacts with oxygen and moisture to form rust (iron oxide). Two methods to prevent iron from rusting are: 1) Galvanization: Coating iron with a layer of zinc, which acts as a sacrificial anode and prevents oxygen from reaching the iron. 2) Painting: Applying a protective layer of paint on the iron surface to prevent contact with oxygen and moisture, thus inhibiting the rusting process."
