     "answer": "Nutrition in human beings involves the process by which food is taken in, broken down, and used by the body for growth, repair, and energy. The process includes ingestion, digestion, absorption, assimilation, and egestion. Ingestion is the intake of food. Digestion begins in the mouth where mechanical breakdown occurs by chewing and chemical breakdown by salivary amylase. In the stomach, food is mixed with gastric juices containing HCl and pepsin, which breaks down proteins. The food then enters the small intestine where complete digestion occurs with the help of pancreatic juices (containing trypsin, amylase, lipase) and intestinal juices (containing erepsin, maltase, lactase, lipase). Bile from the liver emulsifies fats. Absorption of nutrients occurs in the small intestine, which has villi to increase surface area. The absorbed nutrients are then assimilated into cells for various functions. Undigested food is egested through the anus."
