     "answer": "Given: Voltage (V) = 12V, Resistance (R) = 6 ohms. We need to find current (I) and power (P). Using Ohm's law: V = I × R. Therefore, I = V / R = 12V / 6Ω = 2A. The current flowing through the circuit is 2 amperes. Power consumed by the resistor can be calculated using P = V × I. P = 12V × 2A = 24W. Therefore, the power consumed by the resistor is 24 watts."
